WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.593
An explainer video can reach people a slide deck misses, or it can shut them out.

2
00:00:05.643 --> 00:00:08.358
Here's how to make sure it brings more people in.

3
00:00:09.858 --> 00:00:12.004
Text alone asks a lot of the reader.

4
00:00:12.054 --> 00:00:18.681
Video spreads the load across voice and image, and lets people pause, rewind and rewatch whenever they need.

5
00:00:19.681 --> 00:00:22.465
But video isn't automatically accessible.

6
00:00:22.515 --> 00:00:28.388
Missing captions, low contrast, colour-only signals and rushed pacing all shut people out.

7
00:00:28.438 --> 00:00:31.559
Each one is fixable at the slide and script stage.

8
00:00:32.559 --> 00:00:37.805
Say what the chart actually shows, so blind and low-vision viewers can follow too.

9
00:00:37.855 --> 00:00:43.774
Then caption everything, check contrast, and keep body text at 24 point or larger.

10
00:00:44.774 --> 00:00:50.043
Swap a vague 'Results' headline and colour-coded pie for a clear statement and labelled bars.

11
00:00:50.093 --> 00:00:53.725
Now it works with sound or without, and with any colour vision.

12
00:00:55.174 --> 00:01:01.952
On Pro, a.i. directs the video, timing gentle animation to your narration so viewers follow by ear and eye.

13
00:01:02.002 --> 00:01:04.996
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

